= DDKD/PPKK/KİP Is Founded

DDKD/PPKK/KİP are among the Kurdish political organizations established during 1975.

**KİP/DDKD/KÖİP/PPKK is founded**

The bonds holding the fragile T-KDP together finally seem to have snapped. The long-standing left-wing faction of the party under Sait Kırmızıtoprak (nom de guerre Dr. Şivan) has finally formally split with the mainline party, beginning operations with the networks that left the party alongside them. Unlike their former comrades, Kırmızıtoprak's group was very quick to adopt a firmly pro-Soviet stance and establish a legal front named Devrimci Demokratik Kültür Dernekleri (Revolutionary Democratic Cultural Associations, DDKD for short) and has sent an armed core to get guerilla training in camps that belong to Palestinian resistance factions.

While the organisation would simply be known as ''Şivancılar'' (literally ''Şivanists'', named after Kırmızıtoprak's nom de guerre Dr. Şivan), by 1977 they would adopt the name Kürdistan İşçi Partisi (Kurdistan Workers Party, KİP for short, not to be confused with PKK), though the name ''Kürdistan Öncü İşçi Partisi/Partiya Karkerên Pêşeng a Kurdistanê'' (Workers' Vanguard Party of Kurdistan, KÖİP or PPKK for short) has also been used by some members. While their armed actions have been limited so far, the Şivanists have managed to whip the urban working-class and artisans into some manner of political consciousness, with DDKD branches gaining more and more attraction among the populace.

